{"availability":"available","full":"jovian-explorer/VEDA","name":"VEDA","description":"VEDA is an open, multi-mission planetary-science computational laboratory capable of discovering, downloading, processing, analyzing, visualizing, and comparing scientific observations across multiple robotic spacecraft missions and celestial bodies.","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-29T13:46:30Z","updated":"2026-10-10T15:00:39Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://jovian-explorer.github.io/software.html#veda","topics":["esa-psa","nasa-pds","planetary-atmospheres","planetary-science","python","radio-occultation","spice"],"demo":"https://jovian-explorer.github.io/software.html#veda","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T15:05:55.271Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T15:05:55.271Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T15:05:55.271Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T15:05:55.271Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["VEDA is a desktop laboratory for planetary atmosphere and ionosphere data. Pick a planet or moon and a date range, and VEDA finds every product the official archives hold for it across all connected missions. You can then download the products, plot them, derive physical parameters, compare observations and compute the observation geometry with SPICE.","All data shown in VEDA come straight from the mission archives (NASA PDS, ESA PSA, JAXA DARTS, ISRO ISSDC, OPUS) and the instrument teams' research data repositories (Zenodo, BIRA-IASB). Nothing is simulated. Nearly every payload of every mission in VEDA can be searched by date and plotted; the few that cannot (no searchable archive route yet) are listed in DATAPOLICY.md.","VEDA is public and updated continuously (version 0.2.0; changes go to the main branch continuously, and a new build is released about once a month). It is ready for use and for testing; please report problems, wrong results and suggestions through Feedback in the app or on the issue tracker."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jovian-explorer/VEDA/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"18fe3702e60e1aa49638558dc3abc1e4498f3cb5faf009f0b9af44a37d2e4fbd","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T15:05:55.530Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T15:05:55.530Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"VEDA is a desktop laboratory for planetary atmosphere and ionosphere data. Pick a planet or moon and a date range, and VEDA finds every product the official archives hold for it across all connected missions. You can then download the products, plot them, derive physical parameters, compare observations and compute the observation geometry with SPICE.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jovian-explorer/VEDA/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"ISRO's PRADAN portal requires a free account, so VEDA opens it for you to sign in; you download there and use Import downloaded files.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jovian-explorer/VEDA/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"18fe3702e60e1aa49638558dc3abc1e4498f3cb5faf009f0b9af44a37d2e4fbd","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jovian-explorer/VEDA/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T15:05:55.531Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-10T15:00:39Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jovian-explorer/VEDA/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T15:05:55.532Z","hash":"18fe3702e60e1aa49638558dc3abc1e4498f3cb5faf009f0b9af44a37d2e4fbd","originalBytes":25509,"storedBytes":25509,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["veda","data","profiles","archive","every","mars","time","mission","release","any","one","temperature","build","each","local","nasa","pds","venus","download","geometry","open","own","per","profile","against","latitude","their","what","altitude","density","esa","only","pressure","products","set","sets","settings","api","archived","date","expres